Subject: Adreno on mainline kernels: clock, memory, no fake zeros, no crash

On mainline msm (no kgsl) the overlay read 0 for the GPU clock and VRAM
and showed 0 W / 0 MHz for sensors these SoCs do not have.

- GPU clock from the GPU devfreq cur_freq when there is no kgsl.
- VRAM: the game's GPU memory (msm drm-total-memory per client); Adreno
  shares system RAM, so the system-wide VRAM line shows that too.
- CPU/GPU power and the memory clock are left blank when there is no
  sensor, instead of a made-up 0.
- Listing a game's fds no longer throws (process gone or unreadable),
  which took the whole overlay down; the next rescan tries again.

